cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Emerald in your research, please cite it using this metadata.
title: Emerald
authors:
  - name: The Emerald contributors
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/evangelion-research/emerald
abstract: >-
  Emerald is an experimental programming language and C11 compiler for
  programming-language research, focused on type-driven verification and
  machine-checked numerical software: a structural type system with
  intersection and union types, flow narrowing, proof-mode checks, and a
  differentiable tensor runtime with reverse-mode autograd.
keywords:
  - programming-language
  - compiler
  - type-systems
  - formal-verification
  - autograd
